%% Supplementary Fig. 1a: from seven source databases to model-ready sequences (sources: docs/paper/preprocessing.md, data.md, tokenization.md)
%% Stage labels start with "Stage n:", not "n.", which Mermaid would read as a Markdown list.
flowchart TB
    SRC["Seven ICU databases, credentialed access<br/>MIMIC-IV 3.1 (USA); eICU-CRD 2.0 (USA, 208 hospitals);<br/>HiRID 1.1.1 (Switzerland); AmsterdamUMCdb 1.0.2 (Netherlands);<br/>SICdb 1.0.8 (Austria); NWICU 0.1.0 (USA); INSPIRE 1.4.2 (South Korea)"]
    ST["Stage 1: staging<br/>native layouts; Parquet mirror with row-count parity"]
    CL["Stage 2: CLIF tables per database<br/>official ETLs for MIMIC-IV and AmsterdamUMCdb;<br/>mapping-table adapters for the other five; normalized to CLIF 3.0"]
    QA["Stage 3: quality assurance<br/>schema and vocabulary validation; cross-database distribution checks;<br/>reconciliation with the community MEDS pipelines"]
    MD["Stage 4: harmonized MEDS<br/>one subject per adult ICU stay, from 48 h before ICU admission to ICU discharge;<br/>common event codes; canonical units"]
    RU["Uniform rules<br/>hourly medians for monitor streams; one row per infusion rate change;<br/>doses only with weights charted before them;<br/>fields documented later masked until documented"]
    DC["Derived concepts, used as labels only<br/>KDIGO AKI stage; ventilation, vasopressor and RRT episodes;<br/>norepinephrine equivalents; first-day SOFA; Adult Sepsis Event"]
    SP["Splits within each database, grouped by patient<br/>train 80%, tuning 5%, held-out 15%"]
    TK["Stage 5: tokenization<br/>vocabulary fitted on the train split: 25,601 tokens;<br/>value deciles per event code; 12 interval tokens;<br/>the grammar accepts all 409,297 stays; lossless round trip"]
    TR["Train: 327,662 stays<br/>Didymos's training, without task labels;<br/>comparators' training, with labels"]
    TU["Tuning: 20,453 stays<br/>model selection, recalibration"]
    HO["Held-out: 61,182 stays<br/>a test store of 2,000 per database"]
    SRC --> ST --> CL --> QA --> MD
    RU -.-> MD
    MD --> SP --> TK
    MD --> DC
    TK --> TR
    TK --> TU
    TK --> HO
    DC -.->|"labels"| TR
    DC -.->|"labels"| HO
    classDef accent fill:#E3EEF7,stroke:#0072B2,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#000000;
    classDef plain fill:#F0F0F0,stroke:#4D4D4D,stroke-width:1px,color:#000000;
    classDef note fill:#FFFFFF,stroke:#B3B3B3,stroke-width:1px,color:#4D4D4D;
    class MD,TK accent;
    class SRC,ST,CL,QA,SP,TR,TU,HO plain;
    class RU,DC note;
